{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792253550,"nonce":"3jhuI0AjTTHpC7JTQ9d1jlEDZ7A=","title":"Text in a page has no system UI face or generic sans-serif","message":"**What**\n\nSYSTEM_UI is empty on every target but macOS and Windows, and blinc_text's generic sans-serif looks for a short list of installed family names. A page has no installed fonts, so text with no family of its own, system-ui and sans-serif resolve to nothing and are measured with estimates, even when the program has registered a font of its own.\n\n**Fix**\n\nFor wasm, SYSTEM_UI is Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial and Arimo: the first the program has registered. system-ui and text with no family are set in it, and so is sans-serif, which resolve_family maps to it. A program brings Arimo by default and a face of its own by registering one under one of the earlier names. monospace and serif have no face in a page unless the program registers one that blinc_text's fallback list names.\n\n**Limit**\n\nsystem_ui() is looked up once, so the program registers its fonts before any text is created.\n\nNeeded by ashui's wasm work (ashui git-bug 0c8c9a02fd454598cd2c6416e34a2595bb562a525a8e14d298084a672907ed68); builds on 477808515ad825362f2988c55ed3b4a0eea1a61a2bde57052c35954c9df25d12.","files":null}]}